            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The presence package gains no file-opening capability. The static test now covers project.go, and the lock read happens in engine/cmd/procedural_lock.go through the existing session-probe reader.",
              "Reason text from the lock reader is sanitized in engine/capability/presence/project.go. It drops invalid UTF-8, turns control characters into spaces, collapses the text to one line and truncates it to 200 runes, so it cannot inject control characters or exceed workflow bounds.",
              "The lock path is rewritten to its project-relative form before the reason is recorded, in engine/cmd/procedural_lock.go. This keeps the machine path out of the workflow log. A path that appears only as part of some other string is not rewritten. That is not a reachable exploit.",
              "I found no secret handling, authorization, injection or dependency changes. The lock is a project-local file, read the same way the session probe already reads it. The behavior change, where an invalid lock is now reported as unavailable, is the requested C10c behavior."
            ]
          }
        }
