            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "I read all 13 patches and found no concrete production failure mode caused by this candidate.",
              "An invalid lock's reason is cleaned and cut to 200 runes by shortReason in engine/capability/presence/project.go. The detail therefore stays within the observation bound, so workflow creation does not fail on a long reason. Tests cover this.",
              "processProject.ReadLock in engine/cmd/procedural_lock.go never returns an error. A missing working directory or worktree gives the unknown-project reading, and an unreadable lock gives an unavailable observation. Workflow creation and runtime probe degrade gracefully.",
              "The stat of the lock is replaced by a read through the session reader. The caller still bounds the probe with probeWithin, and the lifecycle applies its own probe deadline. A blocking read of an unusual lock file (for example a FIFO) is speculative, and the session probe already has the same exposure, so I am not reporting it.",
              "The path-stripping in withoutLockPath only rewrites the exact lock path. This affects log hygiene only, not availability."
            ]
          }
        }
