            "evidence": [
              "I read all 13 patches. The change replaces the ProceduralLock path field with a ProjectContext port. The adapter that answers the port is in engine/cmd/procedural_lock.go.",
              "The names match what the code does: LockReading, LockState, processProject, withoutLockPath and shortReason. MaxReasonRunes and noReasonGiven are named constants with comments explaining why they exist.",
              "The old stat-based observeProcedural was removed and its replacement is in project.go, so I found no dead or duplicated logic. deps.presenceProber() is now the single place the prober is built for both 'runtime probe' and the workflow verbs.",
              "The doc comments, README, usage text and the tests that check them were updated together. I found no stale comment or misleading description.",
              "One minor point, not worth a finding: processProject.ReadLock resolves the worktree root itself and the reader's Load resolves it again. The adapter comment explains that both use the reader's own function."
