            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R3-001",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/cmd/procedural_lock.go:104-120",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "ReadLock resolves the worktree root, then locks.Load(dir) resolves it again. That is two repo-locator calls per probe, and a worktree change between them could make the root used for path redaction differ from the root the reader used. The window is tiny and the effect is only an unredacted path in a reason.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/cmd/procedural_lock.go:104-120"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "I read all 13 changed paths in the patch.",
              "The presence prober maps each lock state to an observation: valid is available; absent and unknown are unavailable with the earlier wording; invalid is unavailable with the session probe's reason, cleaned by shortReason.",
              "shortReason bounds the reason at 200 runes, one line, valid UTF-8, with no control characters. Unit tests cover those bounds and the edge cases.",
              "I could not confirm that the 44-rune prefix plus 200 runes stays within workflow.MaxObservationDetailLength, because that constant is outside the patch. The tests assert the bound, so a violation would show up there.",
              "The cmd tests compare the create-time record, the runtime probe output and the session probe against the same reader. They also cover the unknown-project cases, the path-redaction cases, the overlong-reason case, and the check that the working directory is read when the prober asks.",
              "The static test now includes project.go, so the no-file-open guarantee still covers the new code.",
              "The old stat-only behaviour that reported any regular file as available is deliberately changed, as the change requests."
            ]
          }
        }
      }
